        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-14T13:34:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we want to return `Vec\u003cu8\u003e`, we probably need a struct that wraps the vector and securely zeroes out the data afterward, as the data is highly confidential. However, considering that `OPENSSL_free` already performs this task, I am hesitant to introduce an additional layer that duplicates the same functionality. Anyway, for users external to this module, they only need to use the `as_slice()` API provided by this struct, making the usage indistinguishable between `Buffer` and `Vec`.",
      "parentUuid": "3d619d1c_92b9d733",
